es like Kamala Harris and Joe Kennedy III campaigning for Jones. Hill, however, retains the advantages of incumbency and a dominant fundraising lead, with roughly $3 million on hand to Jones's $200,000. Most expert raters still call the race Likely Republican, and prediction markets give Jones only about an 18 percent chance. The race appears competitive but tilts toward Hill, with affordability and healthcare as the central issues.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3233, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2423, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2933, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3205, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3445, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2683, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2648, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2693, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2922, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2948, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1951, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.2153, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.2896, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.2694, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.2594, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.2672, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.3206, "margin": -3.0}]}